From: Stained Glass OS <dev@stained-glass.example>
Subject: magnify, osk, explorer: Magnifier and the On-Screen Keyboard

Windows has magnify.exe and osk.exe in system32; Wine has neither. As 0120
does for calc.exe, both are launchers (calc's handoff.c) for what App Paths
registers -- sg-shell's Magnifier and On-Screen Keyboard -- with the same
arguments, in system32 and syswow64.

Explorer's keys, as on Windows: Win+Plus (the '=' key or the keypad's +)
starts Magnifier, or, when its window (class SgMagnifier) is open, tells it
to zoom in (WM_COMMAND 0x101); Win+Minus zooms out (0x102); Win+Esc closes
it (WM_CLOSE); without a Magnifier open those two do nothing. Win+Ctrl+O
starts the On-Screen Keyboard, or closes it when it is open (OSKMainClass).

Gate: test/a11y-gate.sh (make test-a11y).
